# Cached parquet and any fetched data. Never committed -- data fetch is a
# separate, cached, offline-first stage and `null audit` must run offline.
# Fetched/derived data is not committed...
data/*
!data/.gitkeep

# ...except the reference caches, which ARE committed on purpose. TRI and OHLCV
# are fetched once from endpoints that can change or block without notice, and
# committing them is what keeps the M7 demo reproducible after that happens.
# Chunks and logs stay out; only the merged parquet and its provenance sidecar go in.
!data/reference/
data/reference/chunks/
data/reference/*.log

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.env

# `null audit`'s default --out is ".", so a manual run from the repo root
# writes verdict.json / evidence.json / report.html / verdict.trials.parquet
# straight into the root. A stray one of these is not clutter -- it's an
# audit artifact of unknown provenance sitting next to the committed ones,
# and a wrong-hash file left there is an integrity hazard, not a convenience.
# Anchored to root only: examples/, service/, and site/ each commit their own
# json/html/parquet audit outputs on purpose and are untouched by this.
/*.json
/*.html
/*.parquet
